WEBVTT

00:00:00.339 --> 00:00:03.647
Unpivoting raises a NULL-policy question.

00:00:03.647 --> 00:00:06.997
You can preserve rows whose value is NULL.

00:00:06.997 --> 00:00:11.392
That keeps the category present and marks the measurement missing.

00:00:11.392 --> 00:00:15.107
Or you can drop NULL rows after unpivoting.

00:00:15.107 --> 00:00:20.617
The right choice depends on whether missingness itself matters to the analysis.

00:00:20.617 --> 00:00:25.632
After reshaping, NULL and zero may have very different meanings.

00:00:25.632 --> 00:00:32.892
NULL can mean the category did not occur or was not measured; zero can mean it was measured and the value

00:00:32.892 --> 00:00:41.040
was truly zero. Do not replace NULL with zero unless that interpretation is correct for the business question.
